WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.900
summer is the busy season for bazai navismail who along with 
her family makes weaker paper for a living.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:17.900
the raw material is the bark of mulberry trees the production process is long 
and tedious but it's greatly helped by the region's blazing summer heat

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:31.900
before being made into paper the bark is soaked in cold water 
for about 12 hours. it's then peeled and boiled for five
more before being beaten for roughly 20 minutes or so

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.900
then it's fermented, filtrated, molded

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.900
[Music]

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.900
and finally dried in a process all done by hand it could all take 
about two days but the final product is certainly worth

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.900
the wait and effort after an hours long process we now have

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:09.900
the finished product. The xinjiang uyghur mulberry paper is 
very sturdy and features high corrosion resistance this 
means that it is not prone to decay and can actually be 
preserved for thousands of years

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:17.900
Despite there being more modern ways of making 
paper busanov says she wants to make sure the craft which 
has been passed on from generation to

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:33.900
generation lives on. 
"It's a gift from our ancestors. 
My grandfather says we should never stop doing it. 
Paper has a role to play in our society so i hope 
to take up the baton and run it well."

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:43.900
Her son 20 year old bill al has been 
perfecting the craft since he was 5.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:51.900
more and more people are becoming interested in such 
ancient crafts our paper is good for paintings and calligraphy 
It's important to pass down

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:07.900
and provide the people with the best paper possible. 
This is heavy listed as a chinese national intangible 
cultural heritage the government has stepped in to 
protect the tradition and seized tourism as key to 
its efforts one more

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:22.900
it has helped create special mulberry paper workshops 
for visitors and develop what's called a craft 
inheritance center in moyu county where locals can 
sell paper as well as other products chuck tientes 
